<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/new-zealand"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/New%20Zealand.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>New Zealand</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Nuclear Free Zone Act passed; te reo Māori becomes an official language</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-china"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20China.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of China</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Martial law on Taiwan is lifted after 38 years</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/moche"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Moche.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Moche</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Walter Alva excavates the intact tomb of the Lord of Sipán at Huaca Rajada</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/presidential-democracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Presidential%20democracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Presidential democracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After mass protests, South Korea adopts a constitution with direct presidential elections</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/derg"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Derg.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Derg</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 22 February the Derg government ends after a referendum approves the constitution of the People's Democratic Republic of Ethiopia; the Derg is formally abolished in September, its members keeping power.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/language/hawaiian"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hawaiian.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hawaiian</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Hawaiian is again allowed as a medium of instruction in public schools, after 91 years</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/forbidden-city"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Forbidden%20City.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Forbidden City</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">UNESCO declares it a World Heritage Site as the Imperial Palace of the Ming and Qing Dynasties</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/hadrians-wall"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hadrian's%20Wall.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hadrian's Wall</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The wall was declared a World Heritage Site</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/ishtar-gate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ishtar%20Gate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ishtar Gate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A smaller reproduction of the gate, built under Saddam Hussein, was completed in Iraq</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/mogao-caves"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mogao%20Caves.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mogao Caves</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Mogao Caves became a UNESCO World Heritage Site</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/santeria"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Santer%C3%ADa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Santería</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Ooni of Ife Olubuse II visits Cuba, reinforcing links with Yoruba religion</span></li></ul></section>
